## 5. AI Product MVP

**Core need:** Wrapping a model (or several) reliably, managing cost/latency, handling non-deterministic output

**Stack**
- Frontend: Next.js / React (streaming UI matters — use SSE or the Vercel AI SDK)
- Backend: Thin API layer that orchestrates calls to LLM providers — don't over-engineer this
- Model layer: Anthropic/OpenAI API directly for MVP; only self-host models if cost or data residency force it
- Vector DB (if RAG needed): Pinecone / Supabase pgvector / Chroma — pgvector is often enough for MVP scale
- DB: PostgreSQL for app data (conversations, users, usage)
- Auth: Standard provider
- Observability: Log every prompt/response pair — you'll need this to debug quality issues

**Architecture**
```
[Client: Web/Mobile] -> [API Layer] -> [LLM Provider API]
                              |               |
                              v               v
                       [PostgreSQL]   [Vector DB (if RAG)]
                              |
                              +--> [Logging/Eval pipeline]
```

**Priorities:** prompt versioning (treat prompts like code — track changes), cost monitoring (LLM calls add up fast), graceful fallback when the model errs or times out, feedback loop (thumbs up/down) to know if outputs are good. Skip: fine-tuning your own model, complex agent frameworks, multi-model routing — until you've proven the single-model approach isn't good enough.

